body:
[ Ignore ]
On 8.10.4 it is not possible to create the index with a mapping without specifying the dimensions, e.g.

```
$ curl -XPUT localhost:9200/foo-index -u elastic:password -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
{
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "foo": {
        "type": "dense_vector"
      }
    }
  }
}
' | jq .
```

Response:
```
{
  "error": {
    "root_cause": [
      {
        "type": "mapper_parsing_exception",
        "reason": "Missing required parameter [dims] for field [foo]"
      }
    ],
    "type": "mapper_parsing_exception",
    "reason": "Failed to parse mapping: Missing required parameter [dims] for field [foo]",
    "caused_by": {
      "type": "mapper_parsing_exception",
      "reason": "Missing required parameter [dims] for field [foo]"
    }
  },
  "status": 400
}
```

and the server logs:
```
[2023-11-21T16:24:27,549][INFO ][o.e.c.m.MetadataCreateIndexService] [chegars-MacBook-Pro.local] failed on parsing mappings on index creation [foo-index]org.elasticsearch.index.mapper.MapperParsingException: Failed to parse mapping: Missing required parameter [dims] for field [foo]
at org.elasticsearch.server@8.10.4/org.elasticsearch.index.mapper.MapperService.parseMapping(MapperService.java:400)
at org.elasticsearch.server@8.10.4/org.elasticsearch.index.mapper.MapperService.merge(MapperService.java:376)
at org.elasticsearch.server@8.10.4/org.elasticsearch.cluster.metadata.MetadataCreateIndexService.updateIndexMappingsAndBuildSortOrder(MetadataCreateIndexService.java:1339)
at org.elasticsearch.server@8.10.4/org.elasticsearch.cluster.metadata.MetadataCreateIndexService.lambda$applyCreateIndexWithTemporaryService$2(MetadataCreateIndexService.java:472)
at org.elasticsearch.server@8.10.4/org.elasticsearch.indices.IndicesService.withTempIndexService(IndicesService.java:731)
```
